{:id "0028-lab-poses"
 :title "Lab: the draft becomes a frame of letter poses, as a pure function of time"
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Every frame of the typing lab is computed, not simulated: given the
        draft and the time, return where each letter is, how it is turned,
        how big, how bright and how much it wobbles. Letters spring in as
        they are typed, finished words play their cue, deleted letters
        drift away as embers, and everything settles exactly onto the
        layout. Renderers (ours, or Jon's) only draw these frames."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"]
 :design "New namespace halfahead.lab.pose (.cljc, pure). Shapes:
          :ha/draft, :ha/glyph-pose, :ha/glyph-frame in halfahead.schema.

          (layout chars advance width-em) -> [{:x :y} ...], one per char.
            Units are em. Left-aligned from x 0; a line breaks at a newline,
            or before a word that would cross width-em (a word longer than
            the width breaks anywhere). Line n has y = -1.35 * n.
            advance is a fn char -> em width; (default-advance c) returns
            0.6 for everything (tests and fallback).

          (frame draft t-ms opts) -> a valid :ha/glyph-frame
            opts: {:advance fn :width-em n :reduced-motion? b}
            Live glyphs: one pose per glyph, in order, :ghost? false, its
            base at the layout position, z 0, no rotation, scale 1,
            opacity 1, glow 0, wobble 0, plus motion:
            - Birth: age a = t - born-ms. Scale follows an underdamped
              spring from 0 to 1 (closed form; overshoot about 15%,
              settled within 400 ms); z starts at 0.6 and springs to 0;
              opacity rises 0 -> 1 over the first 90 ms.
            - Cues: for each placed cue covering the glyph, local time
              u = t - at-ms - 25 * (position of the glyph within the
              cue). Each effect lasts at most 1400 ms and scales its
              amplitude by the cue's intensity:
                :pop     scale bump to 1.35 and back
                :launch  y arc up 1.2 em with z +1.5, landing with wobble
                         that decays
                :shimmer glow oscillating and decaying, small y float
                :skitter x jitter, deterministic from the glyph id,
                         decaying
                :quake   x/y shake +-0.15 em and a glow flash 1 -> 0
                         (lightning)
                :melt    y droops 0.4 em with rx tilt, springs back
                :rewind  rz from -2 pi to 0, last glyph first
                :fuse    x offset spread outward, converging to 0
                :jitter  small x/y jitter throughout, decaying
                :glow    glow pulse 0 -> 0.9 -> 0
                :wobble  wobble 1 -> 0, decaying
              Effects add; clamp opacity, glow and wobble into [0, 1].
            Ghosts: one pose per ghost younger than 600 ms, :ghost? true, at
            the layout position its :index had in the current text (clamped
            to the end), rising 1.5 em, spinning rz, scale 1 -> 0.6,
            opacity 1 -> 0 over 600 ms (embers). Ghost poses come after the
            live ones.
            Caret: just after the last live glyph's base position (x of
            its base plus its advance; x 0 y 0 for an empty draft).
            Reduced motion: every live pose is exactly its base, and no
            ghost poses.
            Deterministic: equal inputs, equal frames. No randomness; any
            jitter derives from glyph ids.
          Use plain arithmetic only (Math functions via a .cljc-safe
          helper), so the same code runs in the browser and Babashka."
 :acceptance
 ["Property (300+ cases over generated drafts with glyphs, ghosts and
   cues of every effect, and times before, during and after all motion):
   the frame is a valid :ha/glyph-frame (so every number is finite and
   opacity/glow/wobble are in [0,1])"
  "Property: the :char of the live poses, in order, joined, equals the
   draft text"
  "Property (settling): at t >= 1500 ms after the latest born-ms, cue
   at-ms and ghost died-ms, every live pose equals its base exactly (x, y
   from layout; z, rotations, glow, wobble 0; scale and opacity 1) and
   there are no ghost poses"
  "Property: with :reduced-motion? true, at any t, live poses equal their
   bases and there are no ghosts"
  "layout: a newline starts a new line at y -1.35; a word that would cross
   width-em moves whole to the next line; with default-advance, \"ab cd\"
   at width 10 puts d at x 2.4"
  "A :quake cue at t+100 ms gives its glyphs glow > 0 and a nonzero
   offset; at t+1500 ms they are back at base"
  "`bb test` stays green on both hosts"]
 :non-goals
 ["No rendering, DOM, three.js, clock reads or randomness"
  "Do not edit halfahead.schema, lab.draft, or lab.cues"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "DESIGN.md"
           "src/halfahead/perform.cljc" "docs/research/conversation-design.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
